  "description": "GUGWOW crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R -3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C108 H111 Dy4 Fe4 N3 O33,13(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Fe2A (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Dy2B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Fe2B (Fe) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 19 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.987-3.998 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.88-134.48°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C134H150Dy4Fe4N16O33. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
